"ws-header wst-header-structure wst-unknown wst-header ws-header ws-noexport noprint dynlayout-exempt\"><div class=\"wst-header-mainblock wst-unknown-mainblock headertemplate\"><div class=\"wst-header-back searchaux wst-unknown-back\"><div class=\"wst-header-back-arrow\">←</div><div class=\"wst-header-back-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!/H-22\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!/H-22\">H-22</a></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-central-cell wst-unknown-central-cell\"><span class=\"wst-header-title wst-unknown-title\"><span class=\"wst-header-title-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!\">Consider the Consequences!</a></span><div class=\"header-section-text\">H-23</div></span></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward searchaux wst-unknown-forward\"><div class=\"wst-header-forward-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!/H-24\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!/H-24\">H-24</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">→</div></div></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">5008535</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!\">Consider the Consequences!</a> — H-23</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15621227/mw-parser-output/.prp-pages-output\">.mw-parser-output .prp-pages-output .__pagefooter{font-size:smaller}</style><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"43\" data-page-number=\"43\" data-page-name=\"Page:Consider the Consequences! (IA consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/48\" data-page-index=\"48\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Consider&#95;the&#95;Consequences!&#95;(IA&#95;consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/48\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;48\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15620827\">.mw-parser-output .wst-center{text-align:center;margin:0 auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-center.wst-center-nomargin>p{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0}</style><div class=\"wst-center tiInherit\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size:120%;\">H-23</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wst-dhr\" style=\"visibility:hidden; line-height:100%;\">&#160;</div>\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Helen's</span> voyage to China with her very pleasant missionary husband was marred by the knowledge of her mother's terrible loneliness at home. Helen had ensconced Mrs. Rogers in two sunny rooms in a boarding-house, with special attendance guaranteed, the new arrangement costing her brother Simeon no more than it had to support the two women. Mrs. Rogers would be physically as comfortable as she had been with her daughter, but Helen knew that her departure had left her mother indeed bereft.\n</p><p>Helen tried conscientiously to hold this feeling of guilt in her heart, but with five lively stepchildren, two of her own later, the mission work, and a husband to whom she became more and more attached, she really didn't have the time. She sent a diary letter to her mother by every mail steamer and the Franklin missionary society took to meeting in Mrs.&#160;Rogers's sitting room once a month to hear the letters read. They voted two thirds of their annual pledges to the Montgomery Mission, and the letters, later published in book form, were widely circulated.\n</p>\n<div class=\"&#95;&#95;nop wst-nop\"></div>\n<p>&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"44\" data-page-number=\"44\" data-page-name=\"Page:Consider the Consequences! (IA consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/49\" data-page-index=\"49\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Consider&#95;the&#95;Consequences!&#95;(IA&#95;consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/49\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;49\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>The consequence was that the very people who had told Helen it was her duty to stay with her mother instead of going to China now said to Mrs. Rogers, \"How fortunate you are in your daughter!\"\n</p>\n<div class=\"&#95;&#95;nop wst-nop\"></div>\n<p>&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐49pp4\nCached time: 20260920184829\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Header (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐page‐id, vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.136 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.254 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nRevision size: 273/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 5623/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1023/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 11/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 1/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4902/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.065/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1032556/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  242.796      1 -total\n 50.64%  122.940      1 Template:Header\n 31.91%   77.487      1 Page:Consider_the_Consequences!_(IA_consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/48\n 22.59%   54.839      1 Template:C\n 12.66%   30.733      1 Template:Center/s\n  6.24%   15.142      2 Template:Optional_style\n  5.74%   13.934      1 Template:Larger\n  3.16%    7.673      1 Template:Font-size-base\n  2.84%    6.899      1 Template:Dhr\n  2.75%    6.673      1 Page:Consider_the_Consequences!_(IA_consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/49\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID deb3c3c5-b523-11f1-8237-0f7e8dc672d4 -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwikisource:pcache:5008535:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20260920184829 and revision id 15620494. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"
